// Ward — ONE blessed spelling [CR#702.21a]: "Whenever this permanent
// becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter
// that spell or ability unless that player pays [cost]." A TRIGGERED
// ability over the becomes-target event ([CR#601.2c] announce-time),
// resolving to the collapsed `May(Pay(cost))` punisher: the payer
// (`who`) is the targeting stack object's controller ("that player"),
// and the unpaid (`if_not`) branch counters that stack object. The
// engine binds the targeting spell-or-ability as the event OBJECT
// (`EventObject`), so both reads land on the source on the stack, never
// the warded permanent. Any cost-shaped/"toll" ward home is deleted —
// this is the only spelling.
//
// Ward {X} ([CR#702.21b]): the optional `where_x` param carries the X
// definition ("ward {X}, where X is the number of experience counters
// you have" — Minthara, Merciless Soul). It lands on the conferred
// triggered ability's `where_x`, and the toll's `Mana([Variable])` is
// priced when the ward TRIGGER RESOLVES, never locked in as it triggers.
// The param defaults to the inert `0` — a plain
// `Ward(cost: [Mana([Generic(2)])])` has no {X} to price, so the default
// is never read; the template's conditional fragment prints the where-X
// clause only when a caller supplies a real definition.
//
// The inner ability is `Innate` — the rule OF THE KEYWORD, not a second
// card-facing ability beside the Composite; layer-6 removal strips the
// whole Composite, so "loses all abilities" still loses ward.
(
    name: "Ward",
    template: "ward ${cost}${, where X is #where_x#}",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    params: { "cost": Cost, "where_x": Default(Count, 0) },
    body: Composite(
        name: "Ward",
        abilities: [Innate(Triggered(
            event: BecomesTarget(
                what: Ref(This),
                by: ControlledBy(OpponentOf(Ref(You))),
            ),
            where_x: Param(where_x),
            effect: May(
                who: ControllerOf(EventObject),
                effect: Pay([Splice(Param(cost))]),
                if_not: Counter(EventObject),
            ),
        ))],
    ),
)
